DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rraatteecchheecckk and ppppssrraatteecchheecckk functions facilitate rate-limiting of ar‐
     bitrary events.  The former enforces a minimum interval between events
     while the latter enforces a maximum number of events per second.

     The rraatteecchheecckk function compares the current time to the value pointed to
     by _l_a_s_t_t_i_m_e.  If the difference is equal to or greater than _m_i_n_i_n_t_e_r_v_a_l,
     it returns a non-zero value and updates _l_a_s_t_t_i_m_e to the current time.
     Otherwise, it returns zero.

     The ppppssrraatteecchheecckk function first compares the current time to _l_a_s_t_t_i_m_e.
     If at least a full second has passed, the value pointed to by the _c_u_r_p_p_s
     argument is reset to 1 and _l_a_s_t_t_i_m_e is updated to the current time.  Oth‐
     erwise, _c_u_r_p_p_s is incremented and _l_a_s_t_t_i_m_e is left untouched.  In either
     case, ppppssrraatteecchheecckk returns a non-zero value if and only if the updated
     _c_u_r_p_p_s is less than or equal to _m_a_x_p_p_s or _m_a_x_p_p_s is negative.

